# .percolate-ignore — coordinator/lib/ contributing source root for the claude-klabauter
# OSS mirror (rows 6 and 7, `claude-klabauter-lib` / `claude-klabauter-coordinator-lib`, authored sibling-side in
# DoE-claude:setup/publish-targets.portable).
#
# SOURCE_DIR for this file is `claude-klabauter/coordinator/lib/` itself. Patterns are
# SOURCE_DIR-RELATIVE — they carry NO `coordinator/lib/` prefix, or they double-prefix
# and match nothing. Read `coordinator_core/.percolate-ignore`'s MECHANISM
# block for the full single-source explanation; it applies here verbatim.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: the matcher is loaded from the ROW'S OWN source_root
# (`round.py :: _percolate_ignore_matcher`, `Path(staging_dir) /
# ".percolate-ignore"`), never from a parent directory. `coordinator/`
# carries its own `.percolate-ignore`, but NO row sources from `coordinator/`
# itself — the rows source `coordinator/lib` and `coordinator/bin` as
# independent subtrees, so that parent file governs nothing that is actually
# published. Without this file the matcher resolves to an empty pattern list,
# `ignore.matches(...)` is False for everything, and `_smack_clear_recursive`
# unlinks every destination entry including bytecode a prior run wrote —
# forcing a recompile on next use, every round. Measured 2026-08-26:
# 69 source .py, 7 .pyc standing at the destination and reaped every round.
#
# NEGATIVE SPEC: bytecode only. This file is NOT a general exclusion surface
# for this row — `.percolate-ignore` is security-load-bearing on the copy leg
# (leak prevention), and every pattern added here also stops that path being
# swept from the destination. Adding a payload path here hides it from both
# legs at once.

# --- Python build artifacts ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
